/-!
# Uniform annihilation of the negative derived pullback cohomology of a blowup

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal generated by `t` elements, and
`p : X = Proj(⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ) ⟶ Spec A` the blowup of `Spec A` in `I`. A fixed power `Iᶜ`,
depending only on `A` and `I`, annihilates the cohomology sheaf `H^j(Lp^*M̃)` for every
`A`-module `M` and every `j ≤ -t`.

The argument is affine local on `X`. The blowup is covered by the spectra of the affine blowup
algebras `A[I/a]`, `a ∈ I`, and the charts attached to the chosen generators already cover
(`Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_specAffineBlowupι_of_eq_span`). On the chart `Spec A[I/a]` the
derived pullback is computed by a projective resolution `P^•` of `M`: the restriction of
`H^j(Lp^*M̃)` is the sheaf associated to `H^j(A[I/a] ⊗_A P^•)`, which in degree `j = -i` is
`Tor_i^A(A[I/a], M)`. That module is annihilated by a power of `I` independent of `M` and of
`i ≥ t` by Stacks tag 0G9Y, and the sum of the exponents over the `t` charts works for all of
them.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_pow_le_annihilator_homology_derivedPullback`: Stacks tag 0GA0, the
  uniform annihilating power.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_uniform_pow_le_annihilator_tor_affineBlowup`: one power of `I`
  annihilates `Tor_i^A(A[I/a_k], M)` for every chart `a_k` of a chosen generating family, every
  `A`-module `M` and every `i ≥ t`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_specAffineBlowupι_of_eq_span`: the charts attached to a
  generating family of `I` already cover the blowup.
* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecChart_toSpec`: the chart `Spec A[I/a] ⟶ X ⟶ Spec A` is `Spec` of the
  structure map `A → A[I/a]`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.chartHomologyIso`: the restriction to an affine chart of the cohomology of the
  pullback of a complex of associated sheaves is the sheaf associated to the cohomology of the
  base change.

## Implementation notes

The affine model `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec I = Proj (reesGrading I)` of the blowup is used, with
its structure morphism `Stacks.Blowup.toSpec I`; this matches the convention of the section of
the source and the model at which the sibling tag 0G9Z is stated.

Annihilation is stated on sections over an arbitrary open of the blowup, the base-ring element
acting through the structure morphism and the restriction of its global section; the sheaf
condition reduces such a statement to the charts.

The cohomological index is kept general throughout, and converted to the homological index of
`Tor` only in `Stacks.Blowup.chart_homology_smul_eq_zero`, whose statement involves no sheaves.

The chart-wise identification is carried out on the *explicit* complex `p^*P̃^•`, not in the
derived category: the derived pullback of `M̃` is computed by the K-flat complex `p^*P̃^•`
(`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPullbackOfATilde.derivedPullbackTildeSingleIso`), and after that only
the degreewise compatibilities of pullback with composition and of pullback with `~` are needed.
Both are available without any derived input, so no composition isomorphism for derived pullback
is used.

Three spellings of the degreewise module pullback are in play — `Scheme.Modules.pullback f`,
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback f.toLRSHom.toShHom` and
`Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f` for an open immersion. The first two are equal by `rfl`, and
the chart constructions are phrased at the `Scheme.Modules` spelling, because only there does
instance search find additivity of the composites.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G9Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G9Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

